128-bit atomic helpers called only where the host has them, as Unicorn 2.1 has it.

AArch64's CASP, PPC64's LQ/STQ/STQCX. and S390X's CDSG, LPQ, STPQ and CSST have helpers for a
parallel context that call QEMU's 128-bit atomic operations (helper_atomic_cmpxchgo_*_mmu,
helper_atomic_ldo/sto_*_mmu), which exist only on a host with 128-bit atomics (HAVE_CMPXCHG128,
HAVE_ATOMIC128); a 32-bit host — wasm32 — has none, and the translators never call these helpers
there (they stop the run for an exclusive step instead). Unicorn 2.0 left the calls in, behind
assert()s that release builds compile out: libunicorn.so.2 imports the missing functions, and its
dlopen fails ("undefined symbol: helper_atomic_cmpxchgo_le_mmu_aarch64"). Each such body is now
under the host's condition, as in Unicorn 2.1.4 (target/arm/helper-a64.c and
target/s390x/mem_helper.c are 2.1.4's; target/ppc/mem_helper.c keeps 2.0's TARGET_PPC64 layout).

